    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0525" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.0012/526.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Page.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 247
                    of the 15th ultimo and, referring to the last paragraph thereof, pointing out
                    the importance of the conclusion of a naturalization treaty between the United
                    States and Italy at the first opportunity, desires to say that it does not
                    regard the present as a favorable time to approach the Italian Government on the
                    subject of a naturalization treaty.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
